-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Third-party references and their licenses
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

nano/messages.py, nano/records.py, nano/dumps.py
  The System Exclusive frame layout, the Alesis manufacturer and family
  IDs, the function codes, the record sizes, the 8-into-7 bit packing and
  the seven-bit name encoding are transcribed as data, and in part
  derived, from:

    Alesis QS6/QS7/QS8/QSR System Exclusive Specification, Alesis Corp.
    System Exclusive dumps produced by the instrument itself

  Its parameter tables are the next thing to be transcribed from the
  specification; that transcription is not in this distribution yet —
  nano/params.py does not exist.

nano/banks.py
  The five banks, their Bank Select values, the sixteen front-panel
  categories and the hardwired silent program are transcribed as data
  from:

    Alesis NanoSynth Reference Manual, Alesis Corp., 1998

  Facts and interface data, transcribed for interoperability. Neither
  document is redistributed here.

vinsynlib
  The shared base of this family of terminal instrument browsers, and a
  runtime dependency of nanosyned (GPL-2.0-or-later; see its own LICENSE
  and per-file notices), at version 0.4.2. Everything nanosyned once
  carried a copy of now lives there: the settings cache, the favourites
  store, the keymap and legend, the command line, the port listing and
  the backup envelope, which nano/backup.py binds rather than copies.
  vinsynlib carries the copyright of the sibling projects it was
  assembled from — the same ones the transport below is ported from.

nano/bridge.py, nano/favorites.py, nano/config.py, nano/catalog.py
  The transport and UI shape is ported from the sibling projects below,
  which are under the same licence:

    rxved      Copyright (C) 2026  rxved contributors
    p2ked      Copyright (C) 2026  p2ked contributors
    emorphed    Copyright (C) 2026  emorphed contributors
    x5ded      Copyright (C) 2026  x5ded contributors
    s3ked      Copyright (C) 2026  s3ked contributors
    eosed      Copyright (C) 2026  eosed contributors
    k2kremote  Copyright (C) 2026  k2kremote contributors
    mpc2emu    Copyright (C) 2025-2026  mpc2emu contributors

